---
import CampaignCard from "../../components/campaign/CampaignCard.astro";
import CampaignGuideGrid from "../../components/campaign/CampaignGuideGrid.astro";
import CampaignHero from "../../components/campaign/CampaignHero.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { campaignLanding } from "../../data/campaigns/campaignCatalog";
import { graphics } from "../../data/graphics";

const relatedGuides = graphics.filter((guide) => ["/elite-campaigns", "/lre/lysander", "/lre/uthar"].includes(guide.href));
---

<Layout
  title={campaignLanding.title}
  description={campaignLanding.description}
  image={campaignLanding.heroImage}
  url="https://terminusmaximus.com/campaigns/"
>
  <Header />

  <main>
    <CampaignHero
      title={campaignLanding.title}
      subtitle={campaignLanding.subtitle}
      image={campaignLanding.heroImage}
      imageAlt="Terminus Maximus Campaign Guides for Warhammer 40,000: Tacticus"
    />

    <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="campaign-guides-heading">
      <h2 id="campaign-guides-heading">Campaign Guides</h2>
      <CampaignGuideGrid />
    </section>

    <section class="content-section" aria-labelledby="campaign-basics-heading">
      <h2 id="campaign-basics-heading">Basics</h2>

      <div class="markdown-content">
        <p>
          Campaigns are the backbone of Tacticus progression. They unlock new characters,
          open additional game modes, and provide a steady source of upgrade materials you'll
          need throughout the game. Whether you're tackling your first Normal campaign or
          pushing into Elite, every stage cleared moves your account forward.
        </p>

        <p class="content-callout">
          <strong>Campaign progress is top priority.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="callout-support">
          New players should focus on stage progression, unit investment, and unlocking
          characters for Campaign more than any other Game Mode.
        </p>

        <p class="content-callout">
          <strong>There is no single "correct" team.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="callout-support">
          These guides are based on successful
          community clears and are designed to minimize your investment, but many different
          teams can complete the same stages.
        </p>

        <h3>Keep in mind</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Required characters</strong> are mandatory, but your supporting heroes often
            have the biggest impact on difficult stages.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Equipment and abilities matter.</strong> A well-equipped character can
            outperform a higher-ranked one with neglected gear.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Every campaign guide</strong> includes recommended teams, equipment priorities,
            enemy overviews, and advice for the most challenging stages.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Don't panic if you're stuck.</strong> Sometimes a single promotion, equipment
            upgrade, or ability level is all that's needed to clear a difficult stage.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Farm as you progress.</strong> Campaigns are one of the best long-term sources
            of upgrade materials, so don't hesitate to replay stages when your roster needs a boost.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          These guides are intended to help you invest wisely, avoid common progression traps,
          and reach Elite Campaigns with the smallest roster investment possible.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section related-section" aria-labelledby="related-guides-heading">
      <h2 id="related-guides-heading">Related Guides</h2>
      <div class="card-grid related-grid">
        {relatedGuides.map((guide) => (
          <CampaignCard
            title={guide.title}
            description={guide.description}
            href={guide.href}
            thumbnail={guide.thumbnail}
          />
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    background: #121212;
    color: #f5f5f5;
    font-family: "Lexend", sans-serif;
  }

  main {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .content-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid #242424;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: #181818;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #333;
    color: #d4af37;
  }

  .card-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 320px));
    justify-content: start;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .markdown-content {
    max-width: 900px;
    color: #cccccc;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .markdown-content h3 {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
    color: #d4af37;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .markdown-content h3:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .markdown-content p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .markdown-content ul {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 1.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.35rem;
  }

  .markdown-content li + li {
    margin-top: 0.65rem;
  }

  .markdown-content strong {
    color: #f5f5f5;
  }

  .content-callout {
    margin: 1rem 0 0 !important;
    padding: 0.8rem 0.9rem;
    border-left: 3px solid #d4af37;
    border-radius: 0 7px 7px 0;
    background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.08);
    color: #f5d76e;
  }

  .content-callout strong {
    color: inherit;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .callout-support {
    margin-top: 0.65rem !important;
    color: #cccccc;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .related-section {
    background: #1e1e1e;
  }

  .related-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .related-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    main {
      padding: 1.25rem;
    }

    .content-section {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .card-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
